 "equipment_type": "Packaged rooftop unit controller (BACnet option)",
 "applies_to": "Carrier Weathermaster 48/50P030-100 single-package large rooftop units with ComfortLink 9.x controls and the factory UPC Open BACnet option.",
 "summary": "On 48/50P large rooftops the BACnet option is a UPC Open controller in its own enclosure below the main control box. It speaks BACnet MS/TP to the BMS and CCN to the unit's ComfortLink board. The list has 169 rows of AVs and BVs: setpoints, air temperatures, pressures and CFM, up to three compressors per circuit, heat relays, economizer, Humidi-MiZer and VFD outputs, thermostat inputs, demand limit switches, alarms and 40 user-defined spare values.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": "ComfortLink 9.x",
 "default_device_instance": "Network number 16101 followed by the MAC address (MAC 20 gives 1610120)",
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Object names end in _1. The CCN point name and default value columns are printed empty.",
  "The table prints AV:2906 twice (User Defined Analog 6 and User Defined Analog 7, user_analog_7_1); the second row is left out here. Analog 8-11 are printed at AV:2907-2910, while the 48/50A list numbers Analog 7-11 as 2907-2911. Check spare user values on the controller.",
  "Ranges are added to descriptions as printed. Units printed as °^F are shown as Δ°F (temperature differences).",
  "The 48/50A list (48-50A-17T) shares most objects but not all (e.g. comm-loss alarm BV:15 there vs BV:105 here, user binaries BV:2911+ vs BV:2951+), so it is a separate entry.",
  "This is ComfortLink + UPC Open, not the SystemVu or SmartVu controls used on other Carrier rooftops."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "Weathermaster 48/50P030-100 Single Package Large Rooftop Units with ComfortLink Version 9.X Controls - Controls, Start-Up, Operation, Service and Troubleshooting (Appendix G: UPC Open Controller Network Points List)",
  "doc_number": "48-50P-15T",
  "revision_date": "3-26",
  "url": "https://brandportal.carrier.com/asset/4dc39d43-803f-422b-8752-1d4064a34adc/48-50P-15T.pdf"
 },
 "integration": {
  "summary": "The BMS talks BACnet MS/TP to the UPC Open, which reads and writes the 48/50P ComfortLink control over CCN. Set the CCN schedule number for the occupancy source you want, then write occupancy, setpoints and (for VAV) the supply air setpoint; read HVAC mode, temperatures and alarm state. Values the BMS feeds in (space, return or outdoor temperature, RH, CO2) are forces that clear if not refreshed.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "BV 2008",
    "name": "occ_status_1",
    "why": "Occupied? (0 = no, 1 = yes); writable"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 3001",
    "name": "occ_cl_stpt_1",
    "why": "Occupied cooling setpoint"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 3002",
    "name": "occ_ht_stpt_1",
    "why": "Occupied heating setpoint"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 3007",
    "name": "sa_temp_stpt_1",
    "why": "Supply air setpoint (VAV units)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 1022",
    "name": "hvac_mode_1",
    "why": "HVAC mode as a number"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 2001",
    "name": "sfan_1",
    "why": "Supply fan relay on/off"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 43",
    "name": "ctrltemp_1",
    "why": "Control temperature (RAT, SPT or zone)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 10",
    "name": "sat_1",
    "why": "Supply air temperature leaving the fan"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 9",
    "name": "alm_1",
    "why": "Unit alarm state"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 105",
    "name": "comm_lost_alm_1",
    "why": "UPC lost CCN communication with the unit"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "Occupancy follows the ComfortLink CCN schedule number (Configuration > CCN > SC.OV > SCH.N): 0 = always occupied, 1 = local schedule (default), 65-99 = a CCN/global schedule. The points list makes Occupied? (BV:2008) writable, but the manual does not describe how a write interacts with SCH.N; test it on site. A remote switch input (RM.CF) can also set occupancy or start/stop the unit.",
  "heartbeat": "The manual says forces at CCN priority 7 clear unless rewritten in time: outside air temperature, outside RH, outside air quality and static pressure reset after 30 minutes, return air and space temperature after 3 minutes.",
  "remote_sensors": "Space Temperature (AV:137), Return Air Temperature (AV:135), Outside Air Temperature (AV:1003), Outside Air RH (AV:119), IAQ (AV:1009) and OAQ (AV:113) are writable. Refresh them within the force timeouts (3 min for space and return temperature, 30 min for outdoor values).",
  "setup": [
   "Set the MAC address on the UPC Open's Tens and Ones rotary switches; the controller reads switches, DIP switches and jumpers only at power-up.",
   "Device instance = network number (default 16101) followed by the MAC address, e.g. MAC 20 gives 1610120.",
   "BAS port: DS3 enable, DS4 E1-485, DS5-DS8 set to MSTP; baud on DS1-DS2 (9600, 19.2k, 38.4k or 76.8k, Carrier default 76.8k); 8N1 fixed. EIA-485 jumpers to EIA-485 and 2W.",
   "Fit a BT485 terminator on the first and last controller of the MS/TP segment.",
   "The UPC Open and the ComfortLink board must use the same CCN element and bus numbers (factory 1 and 0); the CCN side stays at 9600 baud."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "Points depend on unit options (heat type, economizer, Humidi-MiZer, VFDs, expansion boards); objects for options not fitted carry no useful data.",
   "Thermostat inputs (Y1, Y2, W1, W2, G) are writable BVs, but they only act with the thermostat control type (C.TYP 3).",
   "The user-defined analog and binary values are spare objects with no unit function.",
   "UPC programs ship in English units; metric needs the UPC files rebuilt."
  ]
 },
